n? Can use headings. Need likely final essay. Need word count estimate: Need maybe 2600 words. Let's draft mentally.\n\nPotential details:\n\nDefine:\n- Observations \\mathcal X, actions \\mathcal A, policies \\Pi=\\mathcal A^\\mathcal X.\n- World model M=(P,G). Variable S_{P-FDT} denotes output of P-FDT's policy-selection function for M. It might be written \\mathrm{P\\text{-}FDT}(\\underline M).\n- Intervention do(S=π).\n- Expected utility of policy:\nEU_{P-FDT}(π) = E[V | do(S=π)] = \\sum_v v P(V=v | do(S=π)).\n- Choice: π^* ∈ argmax_{π∈Π} EU(π). Actual action a^*=π^*(x).\nIf sequential: histories h∈H, π:H→A, trajectories induced.\n\nCompare:\nEDT: argmax_a E[V | X=x,A=a]\nCDT: argmax_a E[V | do(A=a), X=x]\nAction-level FDT (source's main equation): argmax_a E[V | do(FDT(M,x)=a)]\nP-FDT: chooses π before applying x.\n\nNeed mention if observations are affected by policy, do(S=π) changes distribution of X. If actual x is observed, P-FDT does not simply condition on x because x may be evidence about policy output; instead, it treats x as the input to selected policy. If x contains policy-independent information, we can condition on it in P before evaluating policies. This is my operational addition.\n\nExamples calculations:\nNewcomb:\nΠ={one, two}. Predictor accuracy .99.\nEU(one)=.99*1,000,000 + .01*0 = 990,000 (or if one-box only box B; if predictor inaccurate empty get 0). EU(two)=.01*1,001,000 + .99*1,000 = 11,000. Choose one.\n\nSmoking lesion:\nLet p lesion. Policy smoke/refrain. Smoking doesn't affect lesion/cancer; adds 1000 if no lesion? Source had utilities: smoking utility 1000; no cancer 1M. With lesion fatal cancer 99%; no lesion cancer 1%. Actually expected utility difference smoke vs refrain = probability the policy controls action? Source had p? Simpler: If lesion probability q, cancer probabilities; smoking can't affect cancer, so expected cancer term same; smoking adds 1000. P-FDT smokes. Could mention formal: EU(smoke)-EU(refrain)=1000 * P(polic